How to Re-enable Auth in Navigation
1) Restore imports in components/navigation.tsx
   - Un-comment:
     import { getSupabaseClient } from "@/lib/supabase"
     import type { User as SupabaseUser } from "@supabase/supabase-js"

2) Restore state
   - Un-comment:
     const [user, setUser] = useState<SupabaseUser | null>(null)
     const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true)

3) Restore effect to hydrate auth state
   - Un-comment the useEffect block that:
     - calls supabase.auth.getUser() on mount to set initial user
     - subscribes to supabase.auth.onAuthStateChange to keep user in sync
     - unsubscribes on cleanup

4) Restore JSX for auth buttons
   - In both desktop and mobile menus, un-comment the conditional block rendering:
     - loading skeleton
     - if authenticated: Account ("/account") and Dashboard ("/dashboard")
     - if not authenticated: Sign In ("/auth/login") and Get Started ("/auth/signup")

5) Verify environment
   - Ensure .env.local contains valid Supabase credentials listed above
   - Restart dev server after any env changes

Optional Reconnection Points
- If you later want to hide Account/Dashboard while still showing Sign In/Sign Up, render only the unauthenticated branch of the conditional.
- If you want the app to redirect away from protected pages (e.g., /dashboard, /account), those pages already perform user checks via Supabase and will route to /auth/login when unauthenticated.

